// regeneration; everything below it is bindgen output. Regenerate against the
// installed GraphBLAS headers with:
//
// bindgen --default-enum-style=rust --opaque-type GB_Iterator_opaque --allowlist-file /usr/local/include/suitesparse/GraphBLAS.h /usr/local/include/suitesparse/GraphBLAS.h -o /tmp/gb.rs
//
// then splice /tmp/gb.rs in below this comment, dropping its own provenance
// line, and run `cargo fmt` — bindgen does not know about this repo's
// `fn_params_layout = "Vertical"`, so raw output fails the format gate.
//
// `--opaque-type GB_Iterator_opaque` is required, not cosmetic: bindgen
// declines to render that struct field-by-field and emits a one-byte
// `_address` placeholder *together with* a layout test asserting the real
// 224 bytes, which fails to compile. Asking for it as an opaque blob makes
// the two agree. Nothing is lost — GraphBLAS documents the iterator's
// contents as off-limits to applications ("must not use `iterator->`
// directly"), the fast field access is via C macros Rust cannot call anyway,
// and no code here touches a field.

